--- PART 2: THE NULLS ---
  (a) UNIVERSAL-scale reading: the residual is FOOTING-ONLY, no environmental run
      -> rho ~ 0, p ~ ns (the gap would be a constant offset, not a gradient)
  (b) EFFECTIVE/EMERGENT reading: a REAL run -- the LOW-EFE galaxies show the
      LARGEST residual -> rho < 0 (residual falls as g_ext rises)
  MEASURED on the primary axis (e_N_maxclu, SPARC N=35): rho = -0.194, p = 0.2615
  VERDICT ON THE NULLS: the data do NOT prefer (b): the correlation is absent/ns -> consistent with (a) the universal/footing-only reading at the committed amplitudes (see the amplitude caveat)
  AMPLITUDE CAVEAT (registered): the committed SPARC e_N spans only 0.0008-0.039;
    the EFE-shift scale at the top e_N ~ (g_ext)^2/a0 ~ 0.2% of a0 vs the per-galaxy residual MAD 0.22 dex -- the run the emergent reading predicts here is far below the per-galaxy scatter (a starving test)

