VERDICTS:
  V1 THE CORRELATION (per-galaxy a0_eff-deep residual = log10(a0e/a0_DE) vs the committed environment, SPARC N=35): primary axis e_N_maxclu = g_ext/a0 (2M++/MCXC maxclu, gext_vectors_2026): Spearman rho = -0.194, p = 0.2615.  Full axis set: e_N_maxclu (g_ext/a0, 2M++/MCXC maxclu) rho -0.194 (p 0.2615); e_N_noclu  (g_ext/a0, no-cluster) rho -0.189 (p 0.2743); g_ext abs  (m/s^2 = e_N . a0_DE) rho -0.194 (p 0.2615); Nm_host (neighbour count) DEGENERATE (constant in-sample); onepd_2mpp (1-Mpc 2M++ density) rho -0.009 (p 0.9594); dom_share (dominant-structure share) rho -0.071 (p 0.6864); dom_kind (group field, cluster=1) DEGENERATE (constant in-sample).  Extreme face (top-5 vs bottom-5 e_N): -0.426 +- 0.162 dex (-2.63 sigma; LOO drop UGC07261: -0.329 +- 0.222, -1.48 sigma).

  V2 THE SPLITS.  S1 (SPARC at the median e_N = 0.0031): high-EFE half mean residual -0.399 dex vs low-EFE -0.183 dex -> HIGH - LOW = -0.217 +- 0.106 dex, sigma = -2.05, bootstrap 95% CI [-0.423, -0.012], P(diff>=0) = 0.019 (emergent predicts NEGATIVE).  CONFOUND AUDIT: the high-e_N half differs from the low in the registered in-sample driver D (f_dark proxy) by -1.85 sigma, rho(e_N, log10 D) = -0.34, rho(e_N, log10 Mb) = -0.13 -- the split is NOT clean of G208's known f_dark structure.  S2 (field vs group): HI field dwarfs a0e med 1.075 x1e-10 (n=55, full baryons) vs WALLABY group members a0_gas med 6.426 x1e-10 (n=44): raw HI - GROUP = -0.609 +- 0.143 dex (-4.27 sigma) -- CONSTRUCTION-DOMINATED (gas-only vs full-baryon abscissa, +0.78 dex systematic floor, only -0.2 dex of which is G100-registered); the construction-clean within-WALLABY group-vs-field a0_gas diff -0.060 +- 0.127 dex (-0.47 sigma, medians +0.096 dex anti-emergent); the G100 registered last-ring split (high-e_N minus low-e_N, the same environmental face on the RAR directly): -0.207 dex, CI [-0.505, +0.050], p = 0.083 ns.

  V3 C4's KILL TEST -- VERDICT: UNCORRELATED (primary axis) with a direction-correct 2-sigma split candidate -- NOT CONFIRMED WITH THE NUMBERS.  On the fully matched SPARC sample the per-galaxy residual vs e_N_maxclu gives rho = -0.194, p = 0.2615 -- the primary correlation is ABSENT (the universal/foothing reading's expectation) -- and the median-e_N split runs HIGH - LOW = -0.217 +- 0.106 dex (-2.05 sigma, bootstrap P(diff>=0) = 0.019) with the extreme face -0.426 +- 0.162 dex (-2.63 sigma), BOTH in the emergent-predicted direction (low-EFE -> larger residual).  TWO AMPLITUDE/PURITY OBJECTIONS prevent reading that as C4 confirmation: (i) the committed e_N only spans 0.0008-0.039 and the EFE floor shift at the top e_N = (g_ext)^2/a0 ~ 0.15% of a0 (6.52e-04 dex) vs a per-galaxy residual MAD 0.22 dex -- the observed 0.22-dex split is ~332x LARGER than the emergent/rho_Lambda amplitude budget (if real, it is NOT the EFE channel); (ii) the high-e_N half differs in the registered in-sample driver D by -1.85 sigma (rho(e_N, log10 D) = -0.34), and G208's own F law (log10 a0e = -0.640 + 1.47 log10 D) attributes 57% of the observed split to that D-difference -- the environmental remainder is only -0.09 dex (-0.9 sigma): the split is CONFOUNDED with G208's f_dark structure.  The GROUP/PAIR face (HI field vs WALLABY group members: raw -0.609 +- 0.143 dex, -4.27 sigma, but CONSTRUCTION-DOMINATED -- gas-only vs full-baryon abscissa, +0.78 dex systematic floor; the construction-clean within-WALLABY face -0.060 +- 0.127 dex, -0.47 sigma with anti-emergent medians; G100 registered last-ring split -0.207 dex, p = 0.083 ns) is also null-to-candidate.  C4's kill test therefore: the EMERGENT reading's environmental correlation is NOT confirmed (primary rho null, amplitude-inconsistent candidate, confounded split) and the UNIVERSAL reading is NOT killed -- the data are largely SILENT at the committed amplitudes, with a direction-correct ~2-sigma split candidate on the SPARC face REGISTERED for the large-EFE sample (e_N ~ 0.3-1, the G036/G044 registered boundary) that can actually distinguish.

